  "id": "eusociality",
  "term": "eusociality",
  "definition": "Eusociality is a highly organized social system in which reproduction is divided between reproductive members, such as queens, and non-reproductive workers. The workers give up having their own offspring and instead help raise close genetic relatives, often their siblings.",
